# A refusal to look at a thing known by name belongs to that thing's tree, and folds with it.
#
# A mind asked to look at something already known may turn it down. Nothing of the thing is on the
# trees yet, so the refusal stands alone on the area's card. When another mind then looks at the
# thing, the refusal is hung under it: it is part of what was made of it. Folding the thing's tree
# therefore puts the refusal away too — it used to stay out, a branch of its own beside the fold.
#
# --refuse-focus stands in for the choice judge answering "not this", which --playground never
# does. The rack is looked at on a first visit so that it is known on the second.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --allow-reentry --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Yard" --period noon --refuse-focus --organs encephalon=6

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
advance 12 180

# First visit: one mind turns the rack down, a second looks at it. It is known from now on.
click observe "Test Rack"
choose childhood_memory
advance 12 180
click observe "Test Rack"
choose comradeship
advance 12 180
expect-state trees element "Test Rack"

click exit
wait mode WorldView 120
advance 12 120
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 120
advance 12 180

# Second visit: the rack is named on the card. The first mind refuses it — a refusal standing on
# the card, with no element for it to hang from.
expect-state symbols click observe "Test Rack" in "Test Yard"
click observe "Test Rack"
choose childhood_memory
advance 12 180
expect-state trees refusal area="Test Yard" mind=childhood_memory
expect-no-state trees element "Test Rack"

# A second mind looks at it: the refusal is under the rack now, not beside it.
click observe "Test Rack"
choose comradeship
advance 12 180
inspect trees
expect-state trees element "Test Rack"
expect-no-state trees refusal area="Test Yard"
expect-state trees   refusal mind=childhood_memory
wait
expect ⊘

# Folded, the refusal goes with the rest; unfolded, it is back.
click fold "Test Rack"
wait
expect-state trees folded=yes
expect-not ⊘
click fold "Test Rack"
wait
expect ⊘
quit
